# Machine-readable citation metadata. GitHub reads this file and offers a
# "Cite this repository" button with BibTeX and APA generated from it.
#
# `version` is checked against Cargo.toml, contracts/openapi.yaml and CHANGELOG.md
# by tests/conformance.rs::j19 — the four are declared separately and drift silently.
#
# A file cannot contain the hash of the commit that contains it. The commit belongs
# with the release, not here: the GitHub Release for each tag records the commit and
# the checksum of the archive, and a paper should cite the tag and that commit together.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use SoulAuth in academic work, please cite it as below.
title: "SoulAuth: Actor-native identity infrastructure for Human and AIActor subjects"
abstract: >-
  SoulAuth is self-hosted identity and authentication infrastructure written in Rust.
  It speaks standard OpenID Connect, and takes Actor Identity rather than User as the
  root of the identity model, so a human and an AI actor can each be a first-class
  authenticable subject: a human proves itself with a password, MFA or an external
  identity, an AI actor with an Ed25519 challenge-response, and both converge on one
  authentication core. Authentication is kept strictly separate from authority.
type: software
authors:
  - name: TRANTOR LABS
    address: Singapore
    website: https://soulauth.trantorlabs.sg/
repository-code: https://github.com/TrantorLabs/SoulAuth
url: https://soulauth.trantorlabs.sg/
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-09
keywords:
  - identity
  - authentication
  - OpenID Connect
  - AI agents
  - actor-native identity
  - Rust
